-- title:
--   Tuples with the same multiset differ by a permutation
-- statement:
--   For tuples $a,b:\{1..j\}\to\{1..r\}$, let $\mathrm{sym}(a)$ be the multiset of entries of $a$, with repetitions. Then
--   $$
--   \mathrm{sym}(a)=\mathrm{sym}(b)\iff b=a\circ\sigma\ \text{ for some permutation }\sigma\text{ of }\{1..j\}.
--   $$
--
--   Multiset indices of tuples are exactly the orbits of the symmetric group acting on slots.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/SymmetricIndex.lean#L57-L72

